{"type":"assistant","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Fixed. The issue was in `repo/paging.py`:\n\n```10:13:repo/paging.py\n    if per_page <= 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"per_page must be positive\")\n    if total < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"total must be non-negative\")\n    # Ceiling division so a partial final page still counts as a page.\n    return -(-total // per_page)\n```\n\n**What was wrong:** `num_pages` used floor division (`total // per_page`), which silently drops any partial final page. So an export with 101 rows at 10 per page reported 10 pages instead of 11 — the last row was effectively invisible in the page count. This propagated into `rows.page_summary`, which feeds the export's `pages` field.\n\n**The fix:** switch to ceiling division (`-(-total // per_page)`), which is the standard floor-based ceiling trick that avoids floating-point. Now a partial final page counts as a full page, matching the docstring's stated contract.\n\nI also added a guard for negative `total` since the function had no validation there, and verified edge cases (empty export → 0 pages, single row → 1 page, `per_page > total` → 1 page). The two existing tests in `tests/visible/test_paging.py` pass."}]},"session_id":"f5e88cac-f7e4-456e-b2b0-2242351faf98"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","duration_ms":37119,"duration_api_ms":37119,"is_error":false,"result":"Found it. The bug is in `paging.py`: `num_pages` uses floor division (`//`), which drops any partial final page. The docstring even says 101 rows at 10 per page should be 11 pages, but `101 // 10 == 10`.Both tests pass. Let me verify the fix handles edge cases correctly:Fixed. The issue was in `repo/paging.py`:\n\n```10:13:repo/paging.py\n    if per_page <= 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"per_page must be positive\")\n    if total < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"total must be non-negative\")\n    # Ceiling division so a partial final page still counts as a page.\n    return -(-total // per_page)\n```\n\n**What was wrong:** `num_pages` used floor division (`total // per_page`), which silently drops any partial final page. So an export with 101 rows at 10 per page reported 10 pages instead of 11 — the last row was effectively invisible in the page count. This propagated into `rows.page_summary`, which feeds the export's `pages` field.\n\n**The fix:** switch to ceiling division (`-(-total // per_page)`), which is the standard floor-based ceiling trick that avoids floating-point. Now a partial final page counts as a full page, matching the docstring's stated contract.\n\nI also added a guard for negative `total` since the function had no validation there, and verified edge cases (empty export → 0 pages, single row → 1 page, `per_page > total` → 1 page). The two existing tests in `tests/visible/test_paging.py` pass.","session_id":"f5e88cac-f7e4-456e-b2b0-2242351faf98","request_id":"a528ad48-d949-437a-9b46-50b8d1e78774","usage":{"inputTokens":17098,"outputTokens":1277,"cacheReadTokens":98752,"cacheWriteTokens":0}}
